Restore the TX DDMI fallback for partially calibrated BOB profiles

0001 removed en7572_apply_tx_ddmi_fallback() because the Nokia XG-040G-MD
never used it once the whole profile came from A2.  The Unionman UNG00A
does use it: its 10G EPON A0 page passes en7572_bob_table_valid() because
the analog calibration at 0x80..0xd7 is programmed, but the TSSI words at
0xb4..0xb7 are erased, while the A2 page has them.  MD32 then reports TX
power word 0x0001 (0.1 uW, -40.00 dBm) with a perfectly normal bias
current, and 0001's en7572_calibrated_base() cannot help because A0 is
"valid".

The TSSI calibration is per module, not per wavelength, so copy the four
programmed bytes into the empty slot before the BOB is loaded into DM and
before prepare() writes them to the runtime register.  This is the same
behaviour the driver had before 0001; it is not dead code.

Reproduced on UNG00A at 192.168.32.254: factory A0 TSSI was
0xffffffff, A2 TSSI 0x69de9401, tx_power_dbm -40.00, tx_bias_ma 16.41
and calibration: ready.  Writing the A2 words into runtime register
0x00b4 made the TX power read 0x6adb (+4.4 dBm) without touching the
laser bias, which pins the missing calibration as the only cause.

diff --git a/airoha-pon-frontends/src/airoha-en7572.c b/airoha-pon-frontends/src/airoha-en7572.c
--- a/airoha-pon-frontends/src/airoha-en7572.c
+++ b/airoha-pon-frontends/src/airoha-en7572.c
@@ -153,6 +153,39 @@
 	return has_nonzero && has_non_ff;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The TX DDMI (TSSI) calibration is a per-module measurement calibration, not a
+ * per-wavelength setting, but a board may have only one of the two BOB pages
+ * programmed with it.
+ *
+ * The Unionman UNG00A is such a board: its 10G EPON A0 page has the analog
+ * calibration (IMOD/IAV/APC/ERC/TIA/PGA) but leaves the four TSSI bytes at
+ * 0xb4..0xb7 erased, while A2 carries them. MD32 then reports the TX power
+ * floor (word 0x0001 => -40.00 dBm) even though the laser bias is perfectly
+ * normal. Borrow the programmed copy so the selected profile can report TX
+ * power. The Nokia XG-040G-MD needs the same when it runs from A2 with A0
+ * erased, so keep this independent of which profile prepare() selects.
+ */
+static void en7572_apply_tx_ddmi_fallback(struct device *dev, struct en7572 *en)
+{
+	u8 *a0 = en->bob + EN7572_BOB_A0_BASE;
+	const u8 *a2 = en->bob + EN7572_BOB_A2_BASE;
+	u32 a0_tssi = get_unaligned_le32(a0 + EN7572_BOB_TSSI_CAL_1);
+	u32 a2_tssi = get_unaligned_le32(a2 + EN7572_BOB_TSSI_CAL_1);
+
+	if (a0_tssi != U32_MAX)
+		return;
+
+	if (a2_tssi == U32_MAX) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "BOB TX DDMI calibration is erased in both profiles\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	memcpy(a0 + EN7572_BOB_TSSI_CAL_1, a2 + EN7572_BOB_TSSI_CAL_1,
+	       sizeof(a0_tssi));
+	dev_warn(dev, "BOB A0 TX DDMI is erased; using the A2 TSSI calibration\n");
+}
+
 /* EN7572 reads use a big-endian 16-bit subaddress and repeated start. */
 static int en7572_read(struct i2c_client *client, u16 reg, void *data,
                        size_t len)
@@ -404,6 +437,9 @@
 			dev,
 			"BOB A2 profile is erased; every mode runs from the calibrated A0 profile\n");
 
+	/* A profile can be analog-calibrated yet lack the TX DDMI words. */
+	en7572_apply_tx_ddmi_fallback(dev, en);
+
 	dev_info(dev, "BOB %s: A0=%s A2=%s\n",
 	         loaded ? "loaded from NVMEM" : "using erased fallback",
 	         en->bob_a0_valid ? "valid" : "empty",
